; Regression test for issue #1884: option values in quotes.
; https://github.com/ledger/ledger/issues/1884
;
; An option line in ~/.ledgerrc takes the rest of the line as its value,
; and no shell removes quotes from it.  A value copied from a command
; line, as in the issue, arrives in quotes, and in double quotes a
; literal double quote is written \" -- as in `depth_spacer : \"\"`
; below, the empty string "".  Ledger strips the outer quotes, turns \"
; into " and \\ into \, and leaves other sequences, such as \n, for the
; format.  It strips single quotes too, but processes no escapes in them.
;
; Init files and journals read option lines the same way, so this test
; gives them in its journal: the test harness runs ledger with
; --args-only, which reads no init file, not even one named with
; --init-file.  test/CheckEnvVars.py reads the same line from a
; ~/.ledgerrc.
;
; The balance format is the documented one that the issue quotes, with
; account names in yellow, as in the issue's ~/.ledgerrc, rather than the
; default blue, so the output shows that the option took effect.  `cat -v`
; shows ESC as ^[.

--balance-format "%(justify(scrub(display_total), 20, -1, true, color))  %(!options.flat ? depth_spacer : \"\")%-(ansify_if(partial_account(options.flat), yellow if color))\n%/%$1\n%/--------------------\n"
--register-format '%(payee) %(amount < 0 ? "out" : "in") %(amount)\n'

2024/01/01 Groceries
    Expenses:Food    $50.00
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/15 Books
    Expenses:Books   $25.00
    Assets:Cash

test bal --force-color | cat -v
             ^[[31m$-75.00^[[0m  ^[[33mAssets:Cash^[[0m
              $75.00  ^[[33mExpenses^[[0m
              $25.00    ^[[33mBooks^[[0m
              $50.00    ^[[33mFood^[[0m
--------------------
                   0
end test

; With --flat, the expression yields the empty string "" instead.
test bal --flat --force-color | cat -v
             ^[[31m$-75.00^[[0m  ^[[33mAssets:Cash^[[0m
              $25.00  ^[[33mExpenses:Books^[[0m
              $50.00  ^[[33mExpenses:Food^[[0m
--------------------
                   0
end test

; The register format is in single quotes, so its double quotes need no
; backslashes.
test reg
Groceries in $50.00
Groceries out $-50.00
Books in $25.00
Books out $-25.00
end test
